# Preserve the Portfolio Design

- Treat the existing site as the source of truth for visual and interaction design.
- Before changing or adding a section, inspect adjacent sections and shared styles/components.
- Reuse the established fonts, type scale, colors, spacing, containers, grids, responsive behavior, and component patterns.
- Extend existing classes, tokens, and components where practical instead of introducing near-duplicates.
- Keep new content aligned with the current section hierarchy and visual rhythm.
- Do not restyle existing elements or introduce a new design direction unless the user explicitly requests it.
- When a request requires a visual departure, limit that departure to the requested scope and preserve the surrounding design.
